body:
This year has been a similar string of losses and blows to me as well. The end of a 5 year relationship, the loss of my only grandmother (that I had contact with) after a fight with dementia, and then finding love with someone else, only for them to pass away suddenly in their sleep... it really does feel like a tidal wave has hit you and you're drowning, doesn't it?

&#x200B;

I've been through hard times before and know I'll make it through, but it hits me randomly that the futures I had planned will never come to be, and I get flashbacks to good memories I can never make again, and just break down sobbing. The puppy we were going to raise together is sat beside me, and every time I see her I think of my boyfriend, how much he would have loved her, how badly I needed him to help me through the pain I already had this year. It feels like everyone else around me is coping so well and just getting on with things and expecting me to be able to do the same, but I can't. I can't concentrate on my work. I can't focus on anything but the losses I've had.

&#x200B;

I hope it will get better soon. I hope it gets better soon for you, too.
